<title>GERMANY: Waigel says G7 cooperation on forex functioning.</title>
<headline>Waigel says G7 cooperation on forex functioning.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Friday that cooperation among Group of Seven industrialised nations on foreign exchange rates was functioning.</p>
<p>Waigel also said the Bonn government expected 1997 German economic growth of about 2.4 percent and that &quot;somewhat more&quot; was possible.</p>
<p>Waigel declined to comment to journalists at an event on current foreign exchange rates, but said: &quot;The G7 cooperation is functioning.&quot;</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
